# Party banter at Castle Ravenloft's gates, main floor, chapel and overlook. Each node opens with an `if` gate: the
# node is eligible only while its condition holds. Party members speak only through interjections.

~ banter_gates
if at:castle_ravenloft_gates and not visited:castle_ravenloft_main_floor and name:kip_smudgewick and name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Drawbridge down, gate up, doors wide open. Nobody leaves a door open like that unless they're selling something.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Maybe he's being polite. Sir Pellam always said, assume good manners until you're bitten.
interject tag:blunt: Manners or a trap, we go in ready for both.
endif
-> END

~ banter_invited
if flag.strahd_invitation == "accepted" and not flag.castle_dinner and name:liriel_dawnsong and name:ratatoille
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: I shall say grace at his table. Aloud. I should like to see his face.
interject name:ratatoille: And if there is soup, I am tasting the soup. Purely as research. I must know what four hundred years does to a stock.
endif
-> END

~ banter_dined
if flag.castle_dinner == "dined" and name:thistle and name:ratatoille
interject name:thistle: Ate with my hands at the vampire's table. He watched me the whole time. Smiling.
interject name:ratatoille: The soup wanted salt. Four hundred years to practise, and the soup wants salt.
interject name:thistle: Cook. He was smiling at me.
endif
-> END

~ banter_wine
if flag.crg_dinner_wine_known
interject tag:cheerful: The wine was only wine. Best I've ever had, mind. Is that worse?
endif
-> END

~ banter_affront
if flag.crg_dinner_fight_over and name:wren_featherfoot and name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:wren_featherfoot: He left. He wasn't losing. He moved his sleeve out of the wine and left. Rude.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: I thought we were doing quite well.
interject class:wizard: He was measuring us. Next time he won't leave.
endif
-> END

~ banter_hearth
if flag.crg_ever_hearth_out and not flag.crg_hoard_opened
interject class:rogue: A fire that burns on nothing, in front of a seam in the stone. You don't guard what you don't keep.
endif
-> END

~ banter_hoard
if flag.crg_hoard_opened and name:wren_featherfoot and name:liriel_dawnsong
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Three hundred crowns behind a fire, never touched. Centuries of it. What's he saving up for?
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Nothing. A man with forever doesn't save, Wren. He only keeps.
endif
-> END

~ banter_chapel
if at:castle_ravenloft_chapel and name:liriel_dawnsong and name:kip_smudgewick
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Morning's grace to this house. It was holy ground once, and it still remembers. Someone should pray here honestly.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Is it all right if I come in? With the horns, I mean. I can wait at the back.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: You'll stand at the front, Kip. With me.
endif
-> END

~ banter_overlook
if at:castle_ravenloft_overlook and name:thistle and name:kip_smudgewick
interject name:thistle: You can see the whole valley from up here! Every road. Every roof. Every tree.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Not one orchard, though. The whole valley, and not one orchard. How do people live?
interject tag:blunt: That's why he likes it up here. It's all his.
endif
-> END
